Made by Anatolii Babii
https://antlii.work

RASTR is a free web tool built on p5.js that lets you convert text
into custom bitmap graphics and motion art using Google Fonts and basic geometric shapes.

The tool provides the features to capture graphics as stills or animation in high resolution
and ability to export/import user settings as a preset in JSON format.

To jump in, I recommend checking out the PRESETS section first
to get a feel of the tool's capabilities and quickly make something based on them.

-- NOTES --

The text is automatically wrapping within the canvas, so in case you need
to move the text on a new row, use the /n combination inside the text.

To import any font from Google Font, simply choose Import Google Font
and copy/paste the font name in the respective text box. I would like to note
that some of the fonts just won't load, and I haven't figured out the cause of this problem.
In this case, just download the font and import it to the program using Import Local Font.

BTW, the local font will not be saved when exporting the preset, and it needs to load independently after importing one.

!! IMPORTANT !!

The program's screen update behavior depends on the Loop Length setting
(found in the EXPORT section):

For video export: 
Set Loop Length to your desired video duration (in seconds).
This will trigger the program to update the image on screen in real-time, allowing you to preview the animation.

For static images:
Set Loop Length to 0. This optimizes performance, improves stability, and reduces power consumption
by preventing unnecessary screen updates.

